Subject: Cantor In-Memory Semantic Find P0 Justification

@ [justification_uuid] 4695c08d-691a-462a-b2a1-38b0180058a0
@ [specification_uuid] 2d678732-1b28-4df5-bc4c-00d6d428bc94
@ [source_snapshot_uuid] d9a12c9a-2c94-4fd8-8734-a897c4ae8d2a

& [Decision]
  + promote bounded lexical unit discovery over the sealed in-memory project result rather than importing the SQLite Reader or widening project assembly

& [WhyNow]
  + project assembly can form and validate a multi-document semantic snapshot but a hosted SOP instance cannot yet ask the smallest question of that snapshot
  + exact and prefix discovery is the narrowest query that makes the snapshot inspectable while exercising identity namespace dependency context and pagination semantics

& [Boundary]
  + the caller retains custody of the assembly and request values
  + the query validates the assembly envelope before reading it and returns cloned semantic values plus deterministic receipts
  + package visibility is structural dependency closure only and context filtering is explicit supplied comparison only
  + result sealing and replay provide auditability without making the result an authorization or truth claim

& [RejectedAlternatives]
  + importing query.rs wholesale is rejected because it requires SQLite storage and carries neighborhood completion evaluation list impact and reference surfaces
  + adding persistence or an index now is rejected because it introduces a distinct authority lifecycle and evidence burden
  + promoting rule evaluation now is rejected because lexical inspectability is the smaller prerequisite and expression evaluation already exists separately in the semantic kernel

& [ExpectedLeverage]
  + an instance can assemble supplied SOP content then discover exact or prefixed terms through a fully in-memory auditable chain before any hosted transport or persistence proposal
